     hhccccoonnttrrooll — Bluetooth HCI configuration utility

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     hhccccoonnttrrooll [--hhNN] [--nn _H_C_I___n_o_d_e___n_a_m_e] _c_o_m_m_a_n_d [_p_a_r_a_m_e_t_e_r_s _._._.]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The hhccccoonnttrrooll utility connects to the specified Netgraph node of type HCI
     or the first one found if none is specified and attempts to send the
     specified command to the HCI Netgraph node or to the associated Bluetooth
     device.  The hhccccoonnttrrooll utility will print results to the standard output
     and error messages to the standard error.

     The options are as follows:

     --hh      Display usage message and exit.

     --NN      Show Bluetooth addresses as numbers.  Normally hhccccoonnttrrooll attempts
             to resolve Bluetooth addresses, and display them symbolically.

     --nn _H_C_I___n_o_d_e___n_a_m_e
             Connect to the specified HCI Netgraph node.

     _c_o_m_m_a_n_d
             One of the supported commands (see below).  The special command
             hheellpp can be used to obtain the list of all supported commands.
             To get more information about a specific command use hheellpp
             _c_o_m_m_a_n_d.

     _p_a_r_a_m_e_t_e_r_s
             One or more optional space separated command parameters.  Many
             commands require a remote device address as one of the parame‐
             ters.  The remote device address can be specified as BD_ADDR or a
             name.  If a name was specified then the hhccccoonnttrrooll utility will
             attempt to resolve the name via bt_gethostbyname(3).

